/T (In this context of evolving economic dynamics, other organizations were formed, and existing ones were renovated to promote regional integration and a free-trade environment across the continent: the Central American Integration System \(SICA\) in 1991 \(successor of MCCA\), CARICOM in 1994, and the Andean Community \(CAN\) in 1997 \(as a successor of the Andean Pact\). These initiatives reflected a broader trend of re-engagement with regionalism. Processes of regional integration became intermediary steps for the liberalization \(not exclusively intra-regional, but also inter-regional\) following the European Union process.)
/E (In this context of evolving economic dynamics, other organizations were formed, and existing ones were renovated to promote regional integration and a free-trade environment across the continent: the Central American Integration System \(SICA\) in 1991 \(successor of MCCA\), CARICOM in 1994, and the Andean Community \(CAN\) in 1997 \(as a successor of the Andean Pact\). These initiatives reflected a broader trend of re-engagement with regionalism. Processes of regional integration became intermediary steps for the liberalization \(not exclusively intra-regional, but also inter-regional\) following the European Union process.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
